WEBVTT

00:00:17.790 --> 00:00:19.750
Riche!

00:00:19.750 --> 00:00:21.330
Johann! Dante!

00:00:21.330 --> 00:00:23.960
I'm so glad you're all right.

00:00:26.130 --> 00:00:30.340
It's that quack and...

00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:33.640
...the Hellfire Witch?!

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:39.310
Hand over <i>The Book of Vanitas</i>.

00:00:39.310 --> 00:00:41.600
Do that, and I shall let you live.

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:45.110
Is that an order from your master, Luca?

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:48.400
How disappointing.

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:51.860
The young battle maiden who
dashed across the battlefield,

00:00:51.860 --> 00:00:54.370
mercilessly exterminating her own kind...

00:00:54.370 --> 00:00:59.540
I heard it was a sight so beautiful
that it made one shudder.

00:00:59.540 --> 00:01:03.330
But I never would've
imagined you'd fall so low.

00:01:03.330 --> 00:01:05.040
And your point is?

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:08.760
My point is I'm tired of playing with you.

00:01:10.670 --> 00:01:14.930
Come to think of it,
I've yet to introduce myself.

00:01:14.930 --> 00:01:17.060
My name is Vanitas.

00:01:17.060 --> 00:01:20.810
The Vampire of the Blue Moon
passed on to me his name and his book.

00:01:20.810 --> 00:01:23.400
Yet I'm but a human!

00:01:25.270 --> 00:01:28.610
The Vampire of the Blue Moon
once feasted on my blood.

00:01:28.610 --> 00:01:31.860
Thus imbued with some of his power,

00:01:31.860 --> 00:01:34.820
I was counted among
the Clan of the Blue Moon.

00:01:36.280 --> 00:01:41.080
I had wished to avoid having to use
this power if at all possible, but...

00:01:41.080 --> 00:01:47.920
Hellfire Witch, I shall make an exception
and reveal to you my true form!

00:01:52.720 --> 00:01:55.930
What devilry is this?

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:20.160
As one might expect,
it takes one monster to battle another!

00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:34.550
THE 
CASE
 STUDY 
OF 
VANITAS

00:02:37.220 --> 00:02:42.270
<i>You're pondering the simple things,</i>
<i>pretty much: human emotions, and love?</i>

00:02:42.270 --> 00:02:46.650
<i>I hope one day you'll understand</i>

00:02:46.650 --> 00:02:51.230
<i>Too many wounds have left you</i>
<i>patched together, a miserable sight</i>

00:02:51.230 --> 00:02:56.490
<i>That doesn't even know</i>
<i>the definition of "alive"</i>

00:02:56.490 --> 00:03:04.000
<i>No need to say,</i>
<i>"Just the two of us" or anything</i>

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:12.590
<i>I've a feeling we can understand</i>
<i>each other, and that's fine for now</i>

00:03:14.090 --> 00:03:21.560
<i>I love this world,</i>
<i>and the light only you give me</i>

00:03:21.560 --> 00:03:26.440
<i>Makes the world I see</i>
<i>through these fractured eyes </i>

00:03:26.440 --> 00:03:31.110
<i>Look gleaming and bright</i>

00:03:31.110 --> 00:03:35.690
<i>There's no such thing as a sure thing</i>

00:03:35.690 --> 00:03:40.450
<i>But you can see me, can't you?</i>

00:03:43.950 --> 00:03:49.290
<i>When sky and void meet, look back</i>
<i>because the dreams will come later</i>

00:03:54.800 --> 00:03:57.760
So it was all just a bluff.

00:03:57.760 --> 00:04:02.260
He was buying time until
Thomas Berneux's paralysis wore off.

00:04:02.260 --> 00:04:06.060
Using a curse-bearer like
a chess piece? That's...

00:04:06.060 --> 00:04:10.900
He gut-punched a lady
without a shred of mercy.

00:04:10.900 --> 00:04:13.400
What a jerk.

00:04:15.030 --> 00:04:17.440
I cannot move.

00:04:17.440 --> 00:04:20.030
Stay right there and watch,

00:04:20.030 --> 00:04:23.370
O witch fallen to earth.

00:04:23.370 --> 00:04:27.620
Now it's your turn, slayer of nine.

00:04:27.620 --> 00:04:30.540
You take the form of a wolf

00:04:30.540 --> 00:04:36.170
and haunt moonlit nights,
seeking the living blood of young women.

00:04:36.170 --> 00:04:41.180
Your malnomen is Loup-Garou,
"wolf who hunts crimson."

00:04:51.520 --> 00:04:55.610
I <i>will </i>have this man's true name back!

00:05:15.380 --> 00:05:18.380
Where am I?

00:05:20.550 --> 00:05:23.090
So that's your true name,

00:05:23.090 --> 00:05:27.060
Bucolicus, "he who composes idylls."

00:05:27.060 --> 00:05:28.930
Astounding.

00:05:30.060 --> 00:05:31.480
Oops!

00:05:31.480 --> 00:05:34.900
I was supposed to
cure him in front of Orlok.

00:05:34.900 --> 00:05:36.820
That won't be necessary.

00:05:36.820 --> 00:05:42.280
We shall tell Master Orlok
exactly what transpired here.

00:05:48.410 --> 00:05:50.080
What the devil?

00:05:50.080 --> 00:05:54.790
I paralyzed you, and the Loup-Garou
poison should yet remain.

00:05:54.790 --> 00:05:59.630
It is not...

00:05:59.630 --> 00:06:03.680
It is not over yet. I can still fight.

00:06:05.720 --> 00:06:08.470
Noé, get over here!

00:06:14.140 --> 00:06:16.360
Master Luca!

00:06:16.360 --> 00:06:18.190
Hellfire Witch,

00:06:18.190 --> 00:06:20.980
you do understand your predicament?

00:06:20.980 --> 00:06:24.360
Should you make one false move,

00:06:24.360 --> 00:06:29.910
my minion shall snap the brat's
bony neck in the wink of an eye.

00:06:29.910 --> 00:06:32.910
He really is a massive jerk.

00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:42.880
I can't hear a word
they're saying over there.

00:06:42.880 --> 00:06:45.430
Nab the kid? What for?

00:06:45.430 --> 00:06:48.970
While you keep Luca
or whatever his name is safe,

00:06:48.970 --> 00:06:53.730
I'll use <i>The Book of Vanitas </i>to create
an area that incapacitates vampires

00:06:53.730 --> 00:06:55.730
and try to reason with the witch.

00:06:55.730 --> 00:06:57.860
Is that even possible?!

00:06:57.860 --> 00:07:03.070
Indeed it is. But such power
weighs too heavily on a child's body.

00:07:03.070 --> 00:07:08.320
Hold him still and cover his mouth
so he won't inhale my power.

00:07:08.320 --> 00:07:11.830
And keep your distance but not too far.

00:07:11.830 --> 00:07:17.500
After all, he must bear witness
to our little parley.

00:07:17.500 --> 00:07:22.920
I believe you when you say you can
defeat the Hellfire Witch without a fight!

00:07:29.220 --> 00:07:31.470
After him!

00:07:31.470 --> 00:07:33.520
No, don't!

00:07:33.520 --> 00:07:36.640
I am defeated and will hinder you no more.

00:07:36.640 --> 00:07:41.730
Do with me what you will, but...

00:07:41.730 --> 00:07:44.280
Do not harm my master!

00:07:45.690 --> 00:07:47.780
I beg you.

00:07:55.370 --> 00:07:59.290
I knew the child was your weakness!

00:08:02.540 --> 00:08:07.260
What's with the tears
and that feeble attitude?

00:08:07.260 --> 00:08:12.180
Such weakness is the result
of wishing to protect something.

00:08:12.180 --> 00:08:14.640
But... I like it.

00:08:14.640 --> 00:08:15.470
Huh?

00:08:15.470 --> 00:08:18.770
I take back what
I just said, Hellfire Witch.

00:08:18.770 --> 00:08:20.980
It's true that you've grown weak,

00:08:20.980 --> 00:08:27.190
but that very weakness makes your
beauty shine all the more bright.

00:08:31.820 --> 00:08:33.950
What's this?

00:08:33.950 --> 00:08:36.370
My strength is gone.

00:08:36.370 --> 00:08:40.370
Hellfire Witch, or should I say, "Jeanne,"

00:08:40.370 --> 00:08:44.040
I've become quite intrigued by you.

00:08:52.050 --> 00:08:52.890
What?

00:08:52.890 --> 00:08:54.680
Huh?

00:09:13.820 --> 00:09:17.540
That look only further whets my appetite.

00:09:23.130 --> 00:09:26.250
How magnificent! You are a marvel, Jeanne!

00:09:26.250 --> 00:09:29.130
What is this pounding in my chest?!

00:09:31.300 --> 00:09:34.720
It's so very loud.
I can't take my eyes off of you.

00:09:34.720 --> 00:09:39.220
More, more! I wish to see you
in every way, shape, and form!

00:09:41.140 --> 00:09:43.600
Why, of course! Now I understand!

00:09:43.600 --> 00:09:45.520
It must be...

00:09:45.520 --> 00:09:47.570
...love!

00:09:50.280 --> 00:09:52.200
I have fallen for you.

00:09:52.200 --> 00:09:54.990
I'll love you from this day forth, Jeanne!

00:09:54.990 --> 00:10:00.500
I must possess all of you. Be my bride!

00:10:01.790 --> 00:10:05.040
How dare you!

00:10:05.040 --> 00:10:08.460
What are you doing to Jeanne?!

00:10:10.090 --> 00:10:12.260
Oh my.

00:10:12.260 --> 00:10:14.130
Master Luca!

00:10:19.140 --> 00:10:21.390
We must fall back this day.

00:10:21.390 --> 00:10:24.730
But remember this! I <i>will </i>kill
you when next we meet!

00:10:24.730 --> 00:10:28.190
I will be back, and I <i>will </i>kill you!

00:10:28.190 --> 00:10:30.730
You'll come see me again?!

00:10:30.730 --> 00:10:34.200
I can hardly wait!

00:10:34.200 --> 00:10:36.280
Jeanne, let go of me!

00:10:36.280 --> 00:10:38.120
I'll tear him limb from limb!

00:10:38.120 --> 00:10:40.200
Master Luca, no!

00:10:53.340 --> 00:10:57.850
Looks like things are about
to get interesting, Noé!

00:10:57.850 --> 00:11:01.770
Seriously. What is your deal?

00:11:09.020 --> 00:11:10.520
He's dead.

00:11:10.520 --> 00:11:12.900
Who did this?

00:11:21.080 --> 00:11:26.460
I went through all the trouble to
so utterly corrupt his name for him.

00:11:26.460 --> 00:11:28.170
But no matter.

00:11:28.170 --> 00:11:32.090
Whose name shall I claim next?

00:11:32.090 --> 00:11:34.380
Now then, everyone!

00:11:34.380 --> 00:11:39.680
The delightful Parade of Charlatan
is about to begin!

00:11:50.650 --> 00:11:52.070
Mademoiselle Amelia!

00:11:52.070 --> 00:11:53.780
Monsieur Noé!

00:11:56.490 --> 00:11:57.950
So it's over?

00:11:57.950 --> 00:12:01.410
Of course, I don't believe every word,

00:12:01.410 --> 00:12:06.290
but I shall postpone Amelia Ruth's
execution for the time being.

00:12:06.290 --> 00:12:10.420
However, you shall remain
where I can keep an eye on you.

00:12:10.420 --> 00:12:14.460
I'll have her work as a
live-in maid at Hôtel Chouchou.

00:12:16.670 --> 00:12:19.760
That goes for you, too, human!

00:12:19.760 --> 00:12:23.600
I grant that dubious book
of yours has some power,

00:12:23.600 --> 00:12:27.560
but I've no intention
of turning you loose.

00:12:27.560 --> 00:12:30.520
I take it Thomas Berneux is dead?

00:12:30.520 --> 00:12:34.860
And you've no idea who killed him, do you?

00:12:34.860 --> 00:12:36.320
Now I see.

00:12:36.320 --> 00:12:42.160
You've realized how valuable
<i>The Book of Vanitas </i>and I can be.

00:12:42.160 --> 00:12:45.830
Very well. Use me to your heart's content.

00:12:45.830 --> 00:12:51.630
You'll be able to swiftly resolve
incidents involving curse-bearers.

00:12:51.630 --> 00:12:56.050
And I'll no longer have to
waste time searching for patients.

00:12:58.800 --> 00:13:02.590
Deliver this letter to the
front desk at Hôtel Chouchou.

00:13:02.590 --> 00:13:07.560
Continue to use your room there
while you are here in Paris.

00:13:07.560 --> 00:13:09.810
So you'll be keeping an eye on us?

00:13:09.810 --> 00:13:12.980
Your room? As in me, too?!

00:13:12.980 --> 00:13:17.780
Correct. You're that human's
caretaker, are you not?

00:13:18.820 --> 00:13:19.820
Definitely not!

00:13:19.820 --> 00:13:23.410
Noé's right. I am <i>his </i>caretaker!

00:13:23.410 --> 00:13:26.160
You keep out of this!

00:13:28.160 --> 00:13:32.370
Now, I'll cut to the chase, Amelia.

00:13:32.370 --> 00:13:34.170
Yes?

00:13:34.170 --> 00:13:37.670
Did you see Charlatan?

00:13:37.670 --> 00:13:41.050
Charlatan?

00:13:41.050 --> 00:13:45.220
I learned something interesting
from some of the vampires I've treated.

00:13:45.220 --> 00:13:49.220
Right before they realized
they'd become curse-bearers,

00:13:49.220 --> 00:13:52.770
they had all seen a similar sight.

00:13:52.770 --> 00:13:55.730
They suddenly found
themselves in a thick fog.

00:13:55.730 --> 00:14:01.450
And there, they saw
the Parade of Charlatan.

00:14:01.450 --> 00:14:04.950
Fog? A parade?

00:14:04.950 --> 00:14:10.700
I feel as if I saw something like
what you have described, but...

00:14:10.700 --> 00:14:14.040
Forgive me. I just can't remember.

00:14:14.040 --> 00:14:16.210
No dice, eh?

00:14:16.210 --> 00:14:21.510
Perhaps you could
exam her, Noé Archiviste?

00:14:23.510 --> 00:14:26.260
You know who I am?

00:14:26.260 --> 00:14:30.020
I received a letter from your teacher.

00:14:30.020 --> 00:14:32.600
It included your name

00:14:32.600 --> 00:14:38.480
and a request that I provide
assistance during your stay in Paris.

00:14:38.480 --> 00:14:43.110
Archiviste, the Fangs That Lay Bare Blood.

00:14:52.200 --> 00:14:57.960
Well, Noé? Would you
like to drink my blood?

00:14:57.960 --> 00:15:00.800
Don't worry.

00:15:00.800 --> 00:15:06.510
You'll no longer see
anything if you do drink it.

00:15:09.850 --> 00:15:12.890
Sis, what's Archiviste?

00:15:12.890 --> 00:15:18.480
It's a clan with the power to read
people's memories by drinking their blood.

00:15:18.480 --> 00:15:21.730
But I heard they died out long ago.

00:15:21.730 --> 00:15:28.620
Please, if there is a way to search
my memory, I'd like you to try.

00:15:28.620 --> 00:15:32.580
If there was any way
I could be of service...

00:15:34.250 --> 00:15:36.500
Very well.

00:15:46.930 --> 00:15:50.510
Umm... Monsieur Noé?

00:15:59.520 --> 00:16:03.030
Deeper. I must go deeper.

00:16:06.280 --> 00:16:11.280
I will lay bare that memory,
the one even she has forgotten.

00:16:21.460 --> 00:16:24.590
There. That must be it!

00:16:28.880 --> 00:16:32.140
Hm? Where am I?

00:16:32.140 --> 00:16:36.480
I was on my way home when...

00:16:54.700 --> 00:16:57.500
What is this?

00:17:00.210 --> 00:17:04.590
I bid you welcome...

00:17:04.590 --> 00:17:08.590
...to the Charlatan Parade!

00:17:11.640 --> 00:17:14.390
It is an accursed thing.

00:17:14.390 --> 00:17:18.100
I'm done for if it catches me.

00:17:30.360 --> 00:17:31.950
There you are.

00:17:31.950 --> 00:17:36.660
Now, show me your true name.

00:17:36.660 --> 00:17:38.830
I'll be defiled. I'll be destroyed.

00:17:38.830 --> 00:17:41.330
My life will--!

00:17:46.840 --> 00:17:50.300
Monsieur Noé! What is it?! Monsieur Noé!

00:17:50.300 --> 00:17:53.470
That thing stole it. It was stolen!

00:17:53.470 --> 00:17:56.810
Her true name! That thing was behind it!

00:18:00.640 --> 00:18:03.560
I saw Charlatan.

00:18:03.560 --> 00:18:07.440
I know not whether it was
a dream or whether it was real.

00:18:07.440 --> 00:18:11.400
But that thing corrupted
Mademoiselle Amelia's name,

00:18:11.400 --> 00:18:13.700
I'm sure of it.

00:18:13.700 --> 00:18:19.410
If that dark being is creating
all those curse-bearers,

00:18:19.410 --> 00:18:23.210
it shall pay dearly, mark my words!

00:18:29.380 --> 00:18:32.470
I have heard the entire tale, good people.

00:18:33.880 --> 00:18:37.140
Bonjour! How I've longed to see you, Noé,

00:18:37.140 --> 00:18:39.310
my beloved fiancé.

00:18:39.310 --> 00:18:40.140
Huh?

00:18:40.140 --> 00:18:40.970
What?

00:18:40.970 --> 00:18:42.140
Fiancé?

00:18:42.140 --> 00:18:43.190
No.

00:18:43.190 --> 00:18:47.690
Come now! Why go and spoil the fun?!

00:18:52.030 --> 00:18:54.360
This is Dominique de Sade.

00:18:54.360 --> 00:18:57.990
We're not betrothed.
She is my childhood friend.

00:18:57.990 --> 00:19:01.370
And at her feet is
her attendant, Kreisler.

00:19:01.370 --> 00:19:04.420
Those are real rose petals and flowers?!

00:19:04.420 --> 00:19:07.460
Hello there, Murr! It's been ages!

00:19:07.460 --> 00:19:10.090
Dominique de Sade,

00:19:10.090 --> 00:19:13.970
daughter of the
Marquis de Sade, Lord of Altus.

00:19:13.970 --> 00:19:16.930
You have friends among
the nobility? Imagine that.

00:19:16.930 --> 00:19:21.100
My teacher is her grandfather.

00:19:21.100 --> 00:19:26.150
Count Orlok, please forgive me
for barging in like this.

00:19:26.150 --> 00:19:33.150
No matter. The House of de Sade's
rude behavior predates your generation.

00:19:33.150 --> 00:19:35.450
Such a sharp tongue.

00:19:36.820 --> 00:19:40.830
I'm going to borrow Noé for a bit.

00:19:40.830 --> 00:19:43.750
Domi, wait. Please, Domi!

00:19:43.750 --> 00:19:46.540
I've been invited to a masquerade ball.

00:19:46.540 --> 00:19:48.500
You will escort me.

00:19:48.500 --> 00:19:50.920
Why me? You could take somebody else.

00:19:50.920 --> 00:19:53.800
I'm here because I was worried about you.

00:20:08.480 --> 00:20:11.230
Lord Ruthven will be there tonight.

00:20:11.230 --> 00:20:16.570
Rumor has it he is conducting
his own research on curse-bearers.

00:20:16.570 --> 00:20:22.330
You may even learn more about
that Charlatan you mentioned.

00:20:28.670 --> 00:20:33.960
The barrier, the product of an experiment
gone wrong long ago, or so it's said.

00:20:33.960 --> 00:20:39.050
It's a spatial distortion linking this
world to Altus, the vampires' world.

00:20:45.770 --> 00:20:47.180
Noé!

00:21:01.570 --> 00:21:03.740
Have you lost your mind?!

00:21:03.740 --> 00:21:05.700
Humans weren't meant to cross the--!

00:21:05.700 --> 00:21:08.910
This isn't my first visit to Altus.

00:21:08.910 --> 00:21:13.340
I learned that I can cross the barrier
as long as I'm touching a vampire.

00:21:13.340 --> 00:21:18.220
And thankfully, you took my hand.

00:21:18.220 --> 00:21:20.590
So what's the problem?

00:21:21.720 --> 00:21:25.930
At any rate, let's step outside, Noé.

00:21:25.930 --> 00:21:28.270
Why did you follow us, human?

00:21:28.270 --> 00:21:32.690
Because I knew you wanted
to separate Noé from me.

00:21:35.610 --> 00:21:39.900
You've got that much right.
You really are an enigma, human.

00:21:58.840 --> 00:22:02.680
You get stars in your eyes over here, too?

00:22:02.680 --> 00:22:07.640
This city never changes
no matter how many times I visit.

00:22:07.640 --> 00:22:10.680
Altus Paris.

00:22:14.600 --> 00:22:17.020
The Fangs That Lay Bare Blood

00:23:48.570 --> 00:23:52.030
Night of Mocking Masks
